# starling-quantize recipe: Qwen3-ASR-0.6B, phone "compact" (663 MB vs 1572 MB
# BF16). Encoder and projector Q8_0 (896-wide rows: no K-quants, and Q4_0
# there cost +0.9 pt German); decoder attention v/o and ffn.down Q6_K, the
# other decoder linears Q5_K; tied embedding/lm_head Q6_K. ~454 MB read per
# decoded token. Every decoder at ~4.5 bpw (Q4_K/Q4_0) failed German.
#
# Measured (2026-10-12, FLEURS test, 100 clips per language, paired bootstrap
# vs BF16): en 5.04 % vs 5.23 % (clip -0.02 pt [-0.61, +0.57]), de 6.59 % vs
# 6.59 % (-0.01 pt [-0.74, +0.64]). Matrix and gate: docs/quantization.md,
# "Phone recipes".
#
#   build/starling-quantize --input models/qwen3-asr-0.6b-bf16-exact.gguf \
#       --output models/qwen3-asr-0.6b-k56x8e6.gguf \
#       --recipe quants/recipes/qwen3-0.6b-k56x8e6.recipe \
#       --imatrix models/qwen3_06-calib160.imx
default q8_0
^llm\.embed\.weight$ q6_k
^llm\.blk\.[0-9]+\.(attn\.[vo]|ffn\.down)\.weight$ q6_k
^llm\.blk\. q5_k
